WEBVTT

NOTE English translation of the spoken Hinglish, not a verbatim transcript. Cue timing is automatically aligned and is not human-verified; it can still be wrong.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.980 line:0% position:50% align:center
In Batch 2 we study international air, sea and road travelling
allowance.

2
00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:09.860 line:0% position:50% align:center
The focus is Central Government civilian tours and training.

3
00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:13.080 line:0% position:50% align:center
Check the separate instructions for Railways and the Armed
Forces.

4
00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:17.020 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, do not copy the domestic class for a foreign
tour.

5
00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:21.080 line:0% position:50% align:center
Every example is hypothetical; check the sanction and latest
orders.

6
00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:25.290 line:0% position:50% align:center
Internationally, Level 17 and above is First Class.

7
00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:28.450 line:0% position:50% align:center
Levels 14 to 16 are Business or Club Class.

8
00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:31.210 line:0% position:50% align:center
Level 13 and below is Economy Class.

9
00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:34.490 line:0% position:50% align:center
Check Level 13A as equivalent to Level 13.

10
00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:38.850 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, 13A checks Economy; Level 14 checks Business.

11
00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:42.810 line:0% position:50% align:center
Entitlement, booking and sanction are separate checks.

12
00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:47.520 line:0% position:50% align:center
When the Government bears the fare, use the three authorised
agents.

13
00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:51.540 line:0% position:50% align:center
These are Balmer Lawrie, Ashok Travels and IRCTC.

14
00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:55.520 line:0% position:50% align:center
A private airline is permitted; class and sanction remain
separate checks.

15
00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:58.900 line:0% position:50% align:center
Check the cheapest eligible fare in the chosen three-hour
slot.

16
00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:02.960 line:0% position:50% align:center
Prefer non-stop travel and check the 10% price-band provision.

17
00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:06.960 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, one selected agent is used for all staff on one
tour.

18
00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:09.850 line:0% position:50% align:center
Booking 21 days in advance is encouraged.

19
00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:13.630 line:0% position:50% align:center
For a tour booking less than 72 hours before travel, justify
it.

20
00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:17.070 line:0% position:50% align:center
Give a separate reason for cancellation less than 24 hours
before travel.

21
00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:20.930 line:0% position:50% align:center
A booking 48 hours before travel requires a self-declaration.

22
00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:24.230 line:0% position:50% align:center
Submit the journey-completion certificate within 72 hours
after travel.

23
00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:27.050 line:0% position:50% align:center
For unauthorised booking, check competent relaxation.

24
00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:31.780 line:0% position:50% align:center
Check competent approval and budget before the foreign visit.

25
00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:35.060 line:0% position:50% align:center
Where Screening Committee and Prime Minister approval is
required,

26
00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:38.960 line:0% position:50% align:center
send the proposal 15 days ahead and no later than five days
ahead.

27
00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:43.220 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, a qualifying Secretary-level proposal must be
submitted on time.

28
00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:46.380 line:0% position:50% align:center
Also check exceptions for training and certain delegations.

29
00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:50.870 line:0% position:50% align:center
For some international bodies or agreements, sponsor terms may
apply.

30
00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:54.350 line:0% position:50% align:center
Do not automatically add both sets of allowances.

31
00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:58.730 line:0% position:50% align:center
If the sponsor paid the flight, do not claim the same fare
again.

32
00:01:58.730 --> 00:02:02.550 line:0% position:50% align:center
Visit approval, hospitality and other expenses need separate
checks.

33
00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:06.820 line:0% position:50% align:center
The latest MEA order located is from September 2023.

34
00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:10.760 line:0% position:50% align:center
For a foreign tour from India, the first 14 days are at the
full admissible rate.

35
00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:14.120 line:0% position:50% align:center
The next 14 days are at 75%; subsequent days are at 60%.

36
00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:17.200 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, assume the full rate is 100 dollars.

37
00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:20.040 line:0% position:50% align:center
A qualifying day 15 gives 75 dollars before other adjustments.

38
00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:23.150 line:0% position:50% align:center
Verify partial days and other adjustments separately.

39
00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:27.300 line:0% position:50% align:center
Now consider the different schedule for specified tours by
overseas-posted officers.

40
00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:30.800 line:0% position:50% align:center
The first seven days are full; the next seven days are 75%.

41
00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:33.580 line:0% position:50% align:center
After that, the rate is 50% of the full admissible rate.

42
00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:37.280 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, at a 100-dollar base, day eight is 75 dollars.

43
00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:41.260 line:0% position:50% align:center
Day fifteen is 50 dollars before other applicable adjustments.

44
00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.840 line:0% position:50% align:center
Do not mix the India and overseas schedules.

45
00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:48.850 line:0% position:50% align:center
For a foreign hotel, check the approved panel and actual
rental.

46
00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:52.670 line:0% position:50% align:center
The order includes service charges and taxes in room rental.

47
00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:57.230 line:0% position:50% align:center
In a no-panel city, check the relevant lowest rate in the
capital city.

48
00:02:57.230 --> 00:03:01.970 line:0% position:50% align:center
Non-representational training uses one step lower hotel
entitlement.

49
00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:06.310 line:0% position:50% align:center
For a seminar, confirm the lower step of the normal hotel
panel.

50
00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:09.730 line:0% position:50% align:center
Do not copy the domestic hotel limit into the foreign hotel
rule.

51
00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:13.800 line:0% position:50% align:center
If hotel charges include breakfast, daily allowance is reduced
by 10%.

52
00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:17.940 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, 100 dollars becomes 90 if only this reduction
applies.

53
00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:21.940 line:0% position:50% align:center
A State Guest receiving all meals free gets 25% of the rate.

54
00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:25.580 line:0% position:50% align:center
Tips are not separately reimbursed in addition to daily
allowance.

55
00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:28.980 line:0% position:50% align:center
When deductions overlap, confirm the method with the office.

56
00:03:29.110 --> 00:03:33.970 line:0% position:50% align:center
Foreign daily allowance does not include transport for
official duty.

57
00:03:33.970 --> 00:03:37.690 line:0% position:50% align:center
Necessary and reasonable conveyance can be considered
separately.

58
00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:41.390 line:0% position:50% align:center
The sanction must also specifically provide funds for this
cost.

59
00:03:41.390 --> 00:03:45.530 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, consider an eligible taxi to an official meeting
separately.

60
00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:49.310 line:0% position:50% align:center
A sightseeing taxi does not automatically become an
official-duty claim.

61
00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:52.630 line:0% position:50% align:center
Check the official MEA exchange rate for currency conversion.

62
00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:57.210 line:0% position:50% align:center
The latest MEA order we located is from September 2023.

63
00:03:57.210 --> 00:04:00.770 line:0% position:50% align:center
Level 10 and above checks the full prescribed annexure rate.

64
00:04:00.770 --> 00:04:04.810 line:0% position:50% align:center
For Levels 2 to 9, copies conflict on the percentage reading.

65
00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:09.290 line:0% position:50% align:center
For a Level 7 calculation, verify a legible official copy
first.

66
00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:12.270 line:0% position:50% align:center
Also check later amendments and departmental adoption.

67
00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:15.650 line:0% position:50% align:center
Now consider the standard sea or river steamer table.

68
00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:20.430 line:0% position:50% align:center
Level nine and above is highest; Level three and below is
lowest class.

69
00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:23.890 line:0% position:50% align:center
For Levels six to eight, the lower class applies when there
are two classes.

70
00:04:23.890 --> 00:04:27.970 line:0% position:50% align:center
For Levels four and five, check the two-, three- and
four-class cases separately.

71
00:04:27.970 --> 00:04:32.350 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, on a three-class steamer, Level five checks
middle or second class.

72
00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:35.870 line:0% position:50% align:center
Ask the office about a three-class case for Levels six to
eight.

73
00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:40.510 line:0% position:50% align:center
A separate table applies to qualifying SCI ships between
mainland and islands.

74
00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:44.730 line:0% position:50% align:center
Level nine and above is Deluxe; six to eight is First or A
cabin.

75
00:04:44.730 --> 00:04:48.870 line:0% position:50% align:center
Levels four and five are Second or B cabin; three and below is
Bunk.

76
00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:53.570 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, an eligible Level seven checks A cabin on an SCI
ship.

77
00:04:53.570 --> 00:04:56.990 line:0% position:50% align:center
Do not apply this special table automatically to every private
ferry.

78
00:04:57.150 --> 00:05:01.410 line:0% position:50% align:center
Where transport rates are prescribed, check the pay level.

79
00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:05.330 line:0% position:50% align:center
Level fourteen and above may use a public AC bus.

80
00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:09.670 line:0% position:50% align:center
When an AC taxi is actually used, check the prescribed AC-taxi
rate.

81
00:05:09.670 --> 00:05:13.050 line:0% position:50% align:center
The prescribed auto-rate option also applies to the listed
modes.

82
00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:17.770 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, check the relevant rate when Level fourteen uses
an AC taxi.

83
00:05:17.770 --> 00:05:21.130 line:0% position:50% align:center
For Levels six to thirteen, AC taxi is not permissible under
this table.

84
00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:25.270 line:0% position:50% align:center
For Levels four and five, public bus is allowed but not AC
bus.

85
00:05:25.270 --> 00:05:28.430 line:0% position:50% align:center
For Level three and below, the row specifies ordinary public
bus.

86
00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:32.230 line:0% position:50% align:center
For listed modes such as auto or own scooter, check the auto
rate.

87
00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:36.090 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, Level three checks the actual ordinary bus fare.

88
00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:39.310 line:0% position:50% align:center
Own car is not expressly listed in that lower row.

89
00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:42.430 line:0% position:50% align:center
Route, sanction and proof checks are also needed.

90
00:05:42.590 --> 00:05:47.610 line:0% position:50% align:center
Where neither State nor neighbouring State has a specific
rate, check the fallback.

91
00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:52.930 line:0% position:50% align:center
The 2017 base is 24 rupees per kilometre for own car or taxi.

92
00:05:52.930 --> 00:05:56.230 line:0% position:50% align:center
For auto or own scooter, the base is 12 rupees per kilometre.

93
00:05:56.230 --> 00:06:00.210 line:0% position:50% align:center
After the first 25% increase, those become 30 and 15.

94
00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:04.650 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, 20 kilometres by eligible auto calculates to 300
rupees.

95
00:06:04.650 --> 00:06:08.890 line:0% position:50% align:center
This result is subject to sanction, actual journey and mode
eligibility.

96
00:06:08.890 --> 00:06:13.940 line:0% position:50% align:center
Where there is no rail, AC bus applies for those entitled to
AC Two and above.

97
00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:17.080 line:0% position:50% align:center
For others, check the Deluxe or ordinary bus rule.

98
00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:21.000 line:0% position:50% align:center
On a rail-connected route, public transport fare is capped by
entitled-class train fare.

99
00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:24.900 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, bus fare is 400 and entitled train fare is 500.

100
00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:27.460 line:0% position:50% align:center
In this public-fare example, the cap has not been crossed.

101
00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:30.440 line:0% position:50% align:center
Do not apply that exact clause automatically to
private-vehicle claims.

102
00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:35.130 line:0% position:50% align:center
Road travel by the employee and transfer effects are separate
components.

103
00:06:35.130 --> 00:06:39.130 line:0% position:50% align:center
For Level six and above, the effects base was 50 rupees per
kilometre.

104
00:06:39.130 --> 00:06:43.250 line:0% position:50% align:center
After the first increase, the calculation is 62 rupees 50
paise.

105
00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:46.870 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, consider the ceiling calculation for 50
kilometres.

106
00:06:46.870 --> 00:06:50.110 line:0% position:50% align:center
The calculated result is 3,125 rupees.

107
00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:54.270 line:0% position:50% align:center
Check actual transport, receipts and any applicable exception
separately.

108
00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:56.770 line:0% position:50% align:center
This calculated ceiling is not an automatic payment.

109
00:06:56.770 --> 00:07:01.080 line:0% position:50% align:center
There is a special rule for Government boats and remote
scientific field work.

110
00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:04.940 line:0% position:50% align:center
In a qualifying case, daily allowance can be equivalent to the
food rate.

111
00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:08.540 line:0% position:50% align:center
Check the Head or controlling officer approval and conditions.

112
00:07:08.540 --> 00:07:12.900 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, an approved survey journey on a Government boat
is assessed separately.

113
00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:15.940 line:0% position:50% align:center
Foot mileage and its indexed rate are separate checks.

114
00:07:15.940 --> 00:07:19.460 line:0% position:50% align:center
Detailed sources and pending verification are in the companion
guide.
